% M8-bits-encoding (D-0153): PB conflict analysis over MIXED rows -- an ORDER pivot (a
% width-1 variable, which stays on the order encoding at every threshold) in a row whose
% other term is on the bits encoding at --bits-above 0. Satisfiable (z = 3, b = 1, c = 1,
% w = 7), so every atom's `red` pair is checked over a database that does not prove
% everything.
%
% Nothing is decided at the root. The search takes z first, at its maximum: z = 7 pushes
% b = 0 and c = 0 (each through a row z + 7b <= 10 with z on bits), and the third row then
% needs w >= 10: a conflict. The pivots are b's and c's order literals; their reasons'
% bits blocks are instantiated at z's lower bound (the atom z_ge_7), and the learned row is
% over that atom. z = 6, 5, 4 conflict the same way; z = 3 leaves b free.
var 0..7: z :: output_var;
var 0..1: b :: output_var;
var 0..1: c :: output_var;
var 0..7: w :: output_var;
constraint int_lin_le([1, 7], [z, b], 10);
constraint int_lin_le([1, 7], [z, c], 10);
constraint int_lin_le([-7, -7, -1], [b, c, w], -10);
solve :: int_search([z, b, c, w], input_order, indomain_max, complete) satisfy;
